`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
This task is a good example of the "don't modify what's already correct" guardrail in the instructions: even though I was asked to "find" all five pieces of information as if starting fresh, the actual file-mutation rules only kick in for fields that are absent, null, or blank. Re-deriving and overwriting already-correct values would violate "Do not modify fields that already contain a non-blank value" and risk introducing drift (e.g., swapping a working Maven-hosted sources URL for a GitHub tag URL that might not exist for every future tested-version alias).

Also worth noting: `repository-url` deliberately points at the monorepo root (`spring-projects/spring-boot`), not a module subpath — because `spring-boot-security` isn't an independent repo, it's one Gradle module (`module/spring-boot-security`) inside the single `spring-boot` monorepo, which is exactly why the test-code-url has to carry the `module/spring-boot-security/src/test` path instead.
